Z||000000||theogre||12-17-2000||02:24 PM||||I'm posting this here becuase there are a number of forum members who have mailed me directly with questions. <B>I Don't Mind direct email from forum members.</B> The problem is reducing the amount of spam that I get.  <P>The amount of spam I've been getting of late has increase tremendously. This has forced me to activate both Earthlink's Spaminator filter and a local black hole list in my mail system.<P>The result of this is mail from several spam heavy U.S. domains will no longer be accepted by my mail software.<P>If you send me mail and don't get a responce within a day or 3 then you may be in one of those domains. <B>I am not selectivly ignoring you. It's your mail server causing you trouble.</B><P>At present the big U.S. domains include Yahoo Juno and Hotmail. A number of foriegn domains, mainly ru and jp domains are also being black holed.<P>------------------<BR>Lake Superior? Is that what I stepped in? Sorry.||||reg||4
